.el .ds Aq '
.TH fleetring-cert-client 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-cert\-client \- Issues a client certificate, naming the principal the client acts as
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring cert client\fR [\fB\-\-out\fR] [\fB\-\-ttl\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-dir\fR> <\fIPRINCIPAL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Issues a client certificate, naming the principal the client acts as
.PP
The files are `client.<principal>.crt` and `client.<principal>.key`, in the directory or in `\-\-out`.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The directory with `ca.crt` and `ca.key`

The new files go into it unless `\-\-out` names another.
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Writes the files into this directory instead: a complete TLS directory

The certificate, its key, and a copy of `ca.crt` go into it, created private to you, instead of the authority\*(Aqs directory.
.TP
\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fI<TTL>\fR
How long the certificate lasts: `<n>d`, `<n>h`, `<n>m`, or `<n>s`

7 days by default.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIPRINCIPAL\fR>
The principal\*(Aqs name

A name that starts with `agent\-` may not contain `.`, which is reserved for delegated agents.
